**Add the reactive logic in `<script>`:**
```ts
const initialWorkId = $derived(page.url.searchParams.get('work'));

$effect(() => {
	const org = $selectedOrgStore;
	const user = $userStore;
	if (!org || user.status !== 'ready') return;
	hydrateLibrarySection({ orgId: org.id, personId: user.personId });
});

$effect(() => {
	const state = $librarySectionStore;
	if (state.status === 'no-rights' || state.status === 'no-library') {
		goto('/');
	}
});
```

**Replace the catalog-strip section** near the bottom of the template (the one rendering MiniWorkCard cards) with the `{#if $librarySectionStore.status === ...}` chain per plan lines 1809-1823. The 5 status branches: loading / empty / ready / error / (no-rights/no-library are silent — $effect already navigates).

**Drop `onMount` from imports** if you don't end up using it (plan snippet listed it but $effect covers all reactive setup). Biome will flag unused imports.

### Potential gotchas
- `$state` blocks in Runes: any module-level `$state` needs to live inside a component context. The above `$derived` and `$effect` go in `<script>` block fine.
- `$selectedOrgStore` / `$userStore` / `$librarySectionStore` — Svelte 4 auto-subscription syntax, preserved in Svelte 5. Just works on any `Readable` / `Writable` store.
- `userStore.status !== 'ready'` — actual userStore in `src/lib/auth/userStore.ts` may have different status names. Verify with `pnpm check` after.

